@@ -72,6 +72,24 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `on`, including its
+event arguments and optional context, and returns an `unsubscribe` function for
+that specific registration:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('another-event', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // Cancellation is safe to repeat.
+```
+
+Unlike `off` and `removeListener`, which remove every matching listener,
+`unsubscribe` only removes the registration that created it. It remains safe to
+call after `off`, `removeListener`, or `removeAllListeners`, including when the
+same function is registered again later.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
